bac77\n parent [2]\n author Ethan Meng <ethan\@rapidcow.org> 1779792234 -0500\n committer Ethan Meng <ethan\@rapidcow.org> 1779792372 -0500\n \n 2:  3e90134 !  2:  95bee4b parenthesize this SKIP for consistency\n--- a/3e9013487b3a87d9b1e004fea2938ccc3dca8e87\t2026-05-26 10:29:46.000000000 +0000\n+++ b/95bee4b2cd6ca46fc33b97b78e8b2ad017e9c405\t2026-05-26 10:29:46.000000000 +0000\n\@\@ -1,5 +1,5 \@\@\n-tree c6256aec184352f57b0b294e472085eb2f2bfce6\n+tree 0b336e990f4af380dd331347fa00bca638ae0178\n parent [3]\n author Ethan Meng <ethan\@rapidcow.org> 1779791360 -0500\n committer Ethan Meng <ethan\@rapidcow.org> 1779791386 -0500\n \n 3:  81b79d5 !  3:  0fb1254 t/mean.t: skip boundary tests when no PERL_PRESERVE_IVUV\n--- a/81b79d5c58d8f23e9e94fe9a25df71e8091c6464\t2026-05-26 10:27:50.000000000 +0000\n+++ b/0fb1254b23253dff6bdae63f2c8135eaad57f05a\t2026-05-26 10:56:41.000000000 +0000\n\@\@ -1,8 +1,8 \@\@\n-tree 1332f223b7c57a7fb93966ae19170bc0be0bbf1c\n+tree 63b01ab94fc017a7bdd18340dc01967149feddec\n parent db4fed4ebf2ffd2b81147c6e77096efd2e49eef2\n author Ethan Meng <ethan\@rapidcow.org> 1779786271 -0500\n-committer Ethan Meng <ethan\@rapidcow.org> 1779791270 -0500\n+committer Ethan Meng <ethan\@rapidcow.org> 1779793001 -0500\n \n t/mean.t: skip boundary tests when no PERL_PRESERVE_IVUV\n \n one, and exactly one test fails:\n\nthen in:\n\ncommit 4f2951830a1e5123e89bfcb5fbcea6fc104fdd58\nAuthor:     Ethan Meng <rapidcow\@RCs-T480s.local>\nAuthorDate: Tue May 26 06:16:44 2026 -0500\nCommit:     Git Daemon <git\@RPi-4B.local>\nCommitDate: Tue May 26 06:16:44 2026 -0500\n\n    Receive pack via ssh transport\n    \n    updated:\n      refs/heads/master 6a1aae4..e2dcbd1 (-4+6)\n       3 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)\n    \n    Submitted-by: Ethan Meng <rapidcow\@RCs-T480s.local>\n    From: [fd7a:115c:a1e0::d701:56a0]:57914 (RCs-T480s.tails.endfind.me)\n    Host: [fd7a:115c:a1e0::c601:f526]:22 (RPi-4B.tails.endfind.me)\n\nwith the following changes:\n\nORIG = 6a1aae40914e42d7fe3d8573cc0ccbe6b364147b\nHEAD = 0a310c82b60c13528d9b1abd853ca785cd04413e (e2dcbd1597a308ab5d376808ba6b04ce40bb01aa~2)\n 0:  6a1aae4 =  0:  0a310c8 semicolons please\n 1:  caabb3e =  1:  97bda1b Get rid of useless +n -n tests\n 2:  95bee4b =  2:  2743324 parenthesize this SKIP for consistency\n 3:  0fb1254 !  3:  e26fa13 t/mean.t: skip boundary tests when no PERL_PRESERVE_IVUV\n--- a/0fb1254b23253dff6bdae63f2c8135eaad57f05a\t2026-05-26 10:56:41.000000000 +0000\n+++ b/e26fa13cf3036ffc50529f5fd39bd8e5b596df89\t2026-05-26 10:56:41.000000000 +0000\n\@\@ -57,12 +57,14 \@\@\n \n the careful IV/UV overflow guard i had observed by testing\n integer math turns out to be implemented in commit 16b7a9a47b\n (tags/perl-5.7.1~968, \"faster and 64 bit preserving arithmetic\")\n-that makes it so, when compiled without -DNO_PERL_PRESERVE_\n-IVUV (perl.h:1088), perl would try adding IV/UV together if\n-it doesn't overflow (pp_hot.c:384); and only in that case\n-would it fall through to NV.\n+that makes it so that, when compiled without -DNO_PERL_PRESERVE\n+_IVUV (perl.h:1088), perl would try adding IV/UV together if it\n+doesn't overflow (pp_hot.c:384); and ONLY in that case would it\n+fall through to NV.\n+\n+Previously there was no attempt at remaining integer.\n \n Here is an example on perl 5.6.2 by me (Data::Float from CPAN):\n \n > perl -Iblib/lib -MData::Float=float_hex -MSort::Search=bisectl \\\n\@\@ -144,9 +146,9 \@\@\n 1.8446744073709e+19 +0x1.ffffffffffef2p+63\n 1.8446744073709e+19 +0x1.ffffffffffef2p+63\n Stuck at -e line 4.\n \n-Here is one by claude:\n+Here is one by claude (with edits by me):\n \n > cat infiniteloop.pl\n   #!/usr/bin/env -S perl -l\n   use strict; use warnings;\n\nthen in:\n\ncommit 69c42ad3c3603bb8ffe22d6940414b3c88798b6f\nAuthor:     Ethan Meng <rapidcow\@RCs-T480s.local>\nAuthorDate: Wed Jun 10 18:32:11 2026 -0500\nCommit:     Git Daemon <git\@RPi-4B.local>\nCommitDate: Wed Jun 10 18:32:11 2026 -0500\n\n    Receive pack via ssh transport\n    \n    updated:\n      refs/heads/master 5c74f11..b98bc3a (-126+126)\n       (identical trees)\n      refs/notes/amends 0f64492..8324d85 (+8)\n       5 files changed, 195 insertions(+)\n      refs/notes/commits 4894b6b..f46c694 (+2)\n       4 files changed, 24 insertions(+)\n    \n    Submitted-by: Ethan Meng <rapidcow\@RCs-T480s.local>\n    From: [fd7a:115c:a1e0::ea32:d402]:51266 (RCs-T480s.local.mhfamily.rapidcow.net)\n    Host: [fd7a:115c:a1e0::6e32:6f59]:22 (RPi-4B.river.mhfamily.rapidcow.net)\n\nwith the following changes:\n\nORIG = 5c74f119ea56720fc8c58cf661948a2412f32e28\nHEAD = b98bc3a0b29d64eef584d95a13fcb50b0f503f47\n 0:  5c74f11 =  0:  b98bc3a Remove comment on the exact integer type\n 1:  f0a6223 =  1:  8f6810a align the semicolons and parentheses....\n 2:  07227a8 =  2:  fc33f12 give credit to forum answer for computation of int limits\n 3:  ebe3b57 =  3:  83b4dfc t/mean.t: Defer definitions of IV/UV limits\n 4:  6cc79c1 =  4:  25abb55 t/mean.t: Compute ivmin with decrement\n 5:  1fbd5b1 =  5:  003b40f t/mean.t: Describe the necessity of the IVUV guard\n 6:  c52e8d1 =  6:  c4b4e5c t/mean.t: Start with expected condition in test skips\n 7:  ca8b7c7 =  7:  a6798b3 Move tricky t/mean.t tests down\n 8:  cc04c20 =  8:  e02f45d Stop using constants in t/mean.t\n 9:  8d1b1a0 =  9:  b01952c Change \"failed to load\" => \"can't load\"\n10:  a33dc07 = 10:  93cd561 Remove SKIP from plan skip_all from one other place\n11:  ae72d98 = 11:  2b31748 xlib/tree-search.pl: update comments for BST_leap\n12:  0c08ea7 = 12:  c05a30b xlib/tree-search.pl: document the [TOK, REF] operand form\n13:  b39327e = 13:  6209044 xt/tree-search.t: sparse tree test is no longer TODO\n14:  4af80ef = 14:  220f6b4 Move TODO string out of the subtest scope\n15:  358c737 ! 15:  58e309c xlib/tree-search.pl: reduce \@aref \@bref to scalars\n--- a/358c737a012cae66df531ca6162015410ae2583b\t2026-06-10 00:04:07.000000000 +0000\n+++ b/58e309c9d758109757d2ac39f6eac7c355a61825\t2026-06-10 00:04:07.000000000 +0000\n\@\@ -4,9 +4,9 \@\@\n committer Ethan Meng <ethan\@rapidcow.org> 1781049847 -0500\n \n xlib/tree-search.pl: reduce \@aref \@bref to scalars\n \n-By Claude Fable 5:\n+From Claude Fable 5:\n \n > \@aref/\@bref are only ever used for their counts,\n > so scalars would read clearer.\n \n16:  b666330 = 16:  890d40e xlib/tree-search.pl: refrain from trusting first encounter\n17:  15c24a3 = 17:  92b502b xlib/tree-search.pl: preliminary fix for sparse trees\n18:  6e8cc9f = 18:  6a7740b Consistent-ize xt/tree-search* error messages\n19:  0fe2c9b = 19:  1ba2216 xt/tree-search.t: TODO regression test for sparse trees\n20:  53a4a91 = 20:  481ed37 xlib/tree-search.pl: doc nits\n21:  345f743 = 21:  3e7588f xlib/tree-search.pl: accept falsy strings as node names\n22:  4bd5c3e = 22:  5b43936 Further fixes in main docs\n23:  72bc756 ! 23:  2b63c64 Main pod typos\n--- a/72bc756738ef03f430724bc1d9e9fbd56923d194\t2026-06-09 20:26:18.000000000 +0000\n+++ b/2b63c6406f32b63b7845a359605ffa9ebcbce6c3\t2026-06-09 20:26:18.000000000 +0000\n\@\@ -7,10 +7,10 \@\@\n \n Naturally I'd have Claude proofread the more important guy\n I've been staring at all night too. :)\n \n-Different from 5f0d5d0, I have commentaries in [[ brackets ]]\n-this time!\n+Message by Claude again.  Different from 8d9b2e9 (Cookbook typos)\n+though, I have commentaries in [[ brackets ]] this time!\n ---\n \n Fixed:\n 1. Content error (Terminology, the case-insensitive example): the\n24:  cccc7b6 = 24:  19ca2cf Add a pause to long sentence\n25:  ffed980 = 25:  76e521a Use <=> for binsearch_range \\\@num_array example\n26:  5f0d5d0 ! 26:  8d9b2e9 Cookbook typos\n--- a/5f0d5d031875d76e3ac504deab389e35736a58c8\t2026-06-09 19:48:14.000000000 +0000\n+++ b/8d9b2e93d18217c560e55f0d83a49d586a717ea6\t2026-06-09 19:48:14.000000000 +0000\n\@\@ -8,9 +8,9 \@\@\n New model :o  I was only trying to have it look at Cookbook to\n see if it can understand my writing.... did NOT expect this to\n happen though. XP  (And now I kind of have to commit, sorry...)\n \n-Here's quote from Claude anyways...\n+Here's message from Claude anyways...\n ---\n \n Fixed four things in lib/Sort/Search/Cookbook.pod:\n \n27:  a73745b = 27:  93934fd That said I do want some space here\n28:  b7b1366 = 28:  bdf022a What is with all this extra space....\n29:  9ac5d57 = 29:  2882742 Essay typo\n30:  060bda3 = 30:  57080cc xt/tree-search-cmd: kill ourselves the same way /bin/sh died\n31:  002e6a8 = 31:  543f75d Use 4-space indent properly\n32:  994cef2 = 32:  39337c8 WAIT wait i've said this exact thing already?!?\n33:  330437c = 33:  a224a56 Cut down on the second time we mention this\n34:  278b030 = 34:  51721e9 Reword IVUV arithmetic caveat note a little bit\n35:  e4788be = 35:  60be33d Now we can finally delete this old guy\n36:  d242b02 = 36:  d8ed600 Explain left vs right variants\n37:  7b2f73c = 37:  9274123 Terser expressions\n38:  d70f74f = 38:  5670b33 Elaborate on search orientations\n39:  4ecc6f0 = 39:  d3032d1 Use 2-space indentation consistently in main docs too\n40:  2edd700 = 40:  f5fe334 Binary operations anti-commute, not anti-symmetry\n41:  9f83091 = 41:  e279f8f Remove spurious period before parenthetical\n42:  c5f057a = 42:  4989ec0 \"xlib\" should still probably be part of the NAME\n43:  782f57f = 43:  68f35af Use itemize in SUBROUTINES section too for uniformity\n44:  9404345 = 44:  1e15b89 Prepend leading slash for Plan9 source path\n45:  fd71928 = 45:  865c7c6 Indent literal blocks with 2-space consistently\n46:  3d20fdb = 46:  6898ce7 Document tree-search.pl command-line interface\n47:  1646be4 = 47:  8243a30 PROOF READ\n48:  7c2186d ! 48:  366f077 Document tree-search.pl Perl interface simply\n--- a/7c2186d01b9d97d4aca094439394c69ba8e3817e\t2026-06-09 08:35:13.000000000 +0000\n+++ b/366f07788fd33ce73ac551d8bb124c12f1c2e4af\t2026-06-09 08:35:13.000000000 +0000\n\@\@ -6,4 +6,7 \@\@\n Document tree-search.pl Perl interface simply\n \n I might want to write something about the command-line\n interface... but nah; this will do for now.\n+\n+Also \$_[0] \$_[1] were already loaded into \$atok \$btok,\n+so we can just use those.\n49:  44c20a6 = 49:  0165536 Tear down vanity package namespace\n50:  5241159 = 50:  b412a1a \$[ is 0, damn it!\n51:  1dcd720 = 51:  4836f29 Purge more useless references to \$[\n52:  d8019ad = 52:  070b937 Note numeric warning that comes with this example\n53:  bf84132 = 53:  80a3e33 Remove period from head -1 .mailmap\n54:  385f1b3 = 54:  636fc7a Exclude .mailmap from MANIFEST and source tarballs\n55:  3396372 = 55:  2759595 Hide my CS mail from git-log(1) and friends\n56:  5a257cd = 56:  3426788 Hold xt tests up to the same standards\n57:  668a004 = 57:  78a1c52 Separate import preamble consistently\n58:  a03a774 = 58:  b0b4862 Add recent tests to MANIFEST\n59:  dfa15b3 = 59:  bf819c9 xt/*.t: address quirks for older perls\n60:  0d8d810 ! 60:  8ad4e05 xt/tree-search-cmd: Finish regression test\n--- a/0d8d81003e71fbf44ba6c80f8e2c3f34ad740ab0\t2026-05-28 19:28:58.000000000 +0000\n+++ b/8ad4e057b8677069f25486703e6a1f3f46213556\t2026-05-28 19:28:58.000000000 +0000\n\@\@ -4,9 +4,11 \@\@\n committer Ethan Meng <ethan\@rapidcow.org> 1779996538 -0500\n \n xt/tree-search-cmd: Finish regression test\n \n-Regression test for commit 87e5c21, where we replaced\n+[Message by Claude]\n+\n+Regression test for commit 7a9ae69, where we replaced\n File::Find with true lexicographic find.  Root tree is\n borrowed from the neighboring xt/tree-search.t.\n \n (I had totally forgotten about \"conclude\", so props to\n61:  50619d8 = 61:  0af5c03 xt/tree-search-cmd: basic load test\n62:  fb4613e = 62:  7567e74 Initialize tree-search-cmd boilerplate\n63:  1231bef = 63:  18dfb4f Copy \"t/lib/test-functions.sh\" from HashTree test\n64:  9824040 = 64:  4e80d88 tree-search: sanity check on self\n65:  87e5c21 = 65:  7a9ae69 tree-search find: roll our own lexicograpical sort\n66:  477409e = 66:  35d90cb xlib/tree-search: Fix a few other spots\n67:  17e5196 = 67:  d82d131 Just import all the names please\n68:  fce804a = 68:  739ccca Expose as BST_{leap,delv} as subcommands\n69:  94da660 = 69:  476eda8 tree-search tests fixup\n70:  c752079 = 70:  1e7c8bc xlib/tree-search: fix four bugs; xt/tree-search: add tests\n71:  2a76a85 = 71:  e6c3bb1 BST_leap and BST_delv proof of concept\n72:  010e040 = 72:  1fb49ae Begin another experiment\n73:  b8cad6f = 73:  b986c70 Grammar again\n74:  e032900 = 74:  358f519 01ARRAY: continued for right search\n75:  e2dcbd1 = 75:  d2b319d file => document\n76:  7a928dd = 76:  b2c898f Add dummy files for srcdocs\n77:  0a310c8 = 77:  50b3d26 semicolons please\n78:  97bda1b = 78:  85bb9f5 Get rid of useless +n -n tests\n79:  2743324 = 79:  a8448d4 parenthesize this SKIP for consistency\n80:  e26fa13 ! 80:  0fe077e t/mean.t: skip boundary tests when no PERL_PRESERVE_IVUV\n--- a/e26fa13cf3036ffc50529f5fd39bd8e5b596df89\t2026-05-26 10:56:41.000000000 +0000\n+++ b/0fe077eb2fa366134f9c5e519e5b3a4ca7b9b6a5\t2026-05-26 10:56:41.000000000 +0000\n\@\@ -1,6 +1,6 \@\@\n tree 63b01ab94fc017a7bdd18340dc01967149feddec\n-parent db4fed4ebf2ffd2b81147c6e77096efd2e49eef2\n+parent d58420cb0728424461152065ed91e006dbe34d1e\n author Ethan Meng <ethan\@rapidcow.org> 1779786271 -0500\n committer Ethan Meng <ethan\@rapidcow.org> 1779793001 -0500\n \n t/mean.t: skip boundary tests when no PERL_PRESERVE_IVUV\n"
