nt error (Terminology, the case-insensitive example): the\n 24:  cccc7b6 =  24:  19ca2cf Add a pause to long sentence\n 25:  ffed980 =  25:  76e521a Use <=> for binsearch_range \\\@num_array example\n 26:  5f0d5d0 !  26:  8d9b2e9 Cookbook typos\n--- a/5f0d5d031875d76e3ac504deab389e35736a58c8\t2026-06-09 19:48:14.000000000 +0000\n+++ b/8d9b2e93d18217c560e55f0d83a49d586a717ea6\t2026-06-09 19:48:14.000000000 +0000\n\@\@ -8,9 +8,9 \@\@\n New model :o  I was only trying to have it look at Cookbook to\n see if it can understand my writing.... did NOT expect this to\n happen though. XP  (And now I kind of have to commit, sorry...)\n \n-Here's quote from Claude anyways...\n+Here's message from Claude anyways...\n ---\n \n Fixed four things in lib/Sort/Search/Cookbook.pod:\n \n 27:  a73745b =  27:  93934fd That said I do want some space here\n 28:  b7b1366 =  28:  bdf022a What is with all this extra space....\n 29:  9ac5d57 =  29:  2882742 Essay typo\n 30:  060bda3 =  30:  57080cc xt/tree-search-cmd: kill ourselves the same way /bin/sh died\n 31:  002e6a8 =  31:  543f75d Use 4-space indent properly\n 32:  994cef2 =  32:  39337c8 WAIT wait i've said this exact thing already?!?\n 33:  330437c =  33:  a224a56 Cut down on the second time we mention this\n 34:  278b030 =  34:  51721e9 Reword IVUV arithmetic caveat note a little bit\n 35:  e4788be =  35:  60be33d Now we can finally delete this old guy\n 36:  d242b02 =  36:  d8ed600 Explain left vs right variants\n 37:  7b2f73c =  37:  9274123 Terser expressions\n 38:  d70f74f =  38:  5670b33 Elaborate on search orientations\n 39:  4ecc6f0 =  39:  d3032d1 Use 2-space indentation consistently in main docs too\n 40:  2edd700 =  40:  f5fe334 Binary operations anti-commute, not anti-symmetry\n 41:  9f83091 =  41:  e279f8f Remove spurious period before parenthetical\n 42:  c5f057a =  42:  4989ec0 \"xlib\" should still probably be part of the NAME\n 43:  782f57f =  43:  68f35af Use itemize in SUBROUTINES section too for uniformity\n 44: 