6-06-09 20:26:18.000000000 +0000\n\@\@ -7,10 +7,10 \@\@\n \n Naturally I'd have Claude proofread the more important guy\n I've been staring at all night too. :)\n \n-Different from 5f0d5d0, I have commentaries in [[ brackets ]]\n-this time!\n+Message by Claude again.  Different from 8d9b2e9 (Cookbook typos)\n+though, I have commentaries in [[ brackets ]] this time!\n ---\n \n Fixed:\n 1. Content error (Terminology, the case-insensitive example): the\n 24:  cccc7b6 =  24:  19ca2cf Add a pause to long sentence\n 25:  ffed980 =  25:  76e521a Use <=> for binsearch_range \\\@num_array example\n 26:  5f0d5d0 !  26:  8d9b2e9 Cookbook typos\n--- a/5f0d5d031875d76e3ac504deab389e35736a58c8\t2026-06-09 19:48:14.000000000 +0000\n+++ b/8d9b2e93d18217c560e55f0d83a49d586a717ea6\t2026-06-09 19:48:14.000000000 +0000\n\@\@ -8,9 +8,9 \@\@\n New model :o  I was only trying to have it look at Cookbook to\n see if it can understand my writing.... did NOT expect this to\n happen though. XP  (And now I kind of have to commit, sorry...)\n \n-Here's quote from Claude anyways...\n+Here's message from Claude anyways...\n ---\n \n Fixed four things in lib/Sort/Search/Cookbook.pod:\n \n 27:  a73745b =  27:  93934fd That said I do want some space here\n 28:  b7b1366 =  28:  bdf022a What is with all this extra space....\n 29:  9ac5d57 =  29:  2882742 Essay typo\n 30:  060bda3 =  30:  57080cc xt/tree-search-cmd: kill ourselves the same way /bin/sh died\n 31:  002e6a8 =  31:  543f75d Use 4-space indent properly\n 32:  994cef2 =  32:  39337c8 WAIT wait i've said this exact thing already?!?\n 33:  330437c =  33:  a224a56 Cut down on the second time we mention this\n 34:  278b030 =  34:  51721e9 Reword IVUV arithmetic caveat note a little bit\n 35:  e4788be =  35:  60be33d Now we can finally delete this old guy\n 36:  d242b02 =  36:  d8ed600 Explain left vs right variants\n 37:  7b2f73c =  37:  9274123 Terser expressions\n 38:  d70f74f =  38:  5670b33 Elaborate on search orientations\n 39:  4ecc6f0 =  39:  d3032d1 Use 2-space indentation consistently in main docs too\n 40:  2edd700 =  40:  f5fe334 Binary operations anti-commute, not anti-symmetry\n 41:  9f83091 =  41:  e279f8f Remove spurious period before parenthetical\n 42:  c5f057a =  42:  4989ec0 \"xlib\" should still probably be part of the NAME\n 43:  782f57f =  43:  68f35af Use itemize in SUBROUTINES section too for uniformity\n 44:  9404345 =  44:  1e15b89 Prepend leading slash for Plan9 source path\n 45:  fd71928 =  45:  865c7c6 Indent literal blocks with 2-space consistently\n 46:  3d20fdb =  46:  6898ce7 Document tree-search.pl command-line interface\n 47:  1646be4 =  47:  8243a30 PROOF READ\n 48:  7c2186d !  48:  366f077 Document tree-search.pl Perl interface simply\n--- a/7c2186d01b9d97d4aca094439394c69ba8e3817e\t2026-06-09 08:35:13.000000000 +0000\n+++ b/366f07788fd33ce73ac551d8bb124c12f1c2e4af\t2026-06-09 08:35:13.000000000 +0000\n\@\@ -6,4 +6,7 \@\@\n Document tree-search.pl Perl interface simply\n \n I might want to write something about the command-line\n interface... but nah; this will do for now.\n+\n+Also \$_[0] \$_[1] were already loaded into \$atok \$btok,\n+so we can just use those.\n 49:  44c20a6 =  49:  0165536 Tear down vanity package namespace\n 50:  5241159 =  50:  b412a1a \$[ is 0, damn it!\n 51:  1dcd720 =  51:  4836f29 Purge more useless references to \$[\n 52:  d8019ad =  52:  070b937 Note numeric warning that comes with this example\n 53:  bf84132 =  53:  80a3e33 Remove period from head -1 .mailmap\n 54:  385f1b3 =  54:  636fc7a Exclude .mailmap from MANIFEST and source tarballs\n 55:  3396372 =  55:  2759595 Hide my CS mail from git-log(1) and friends\n 56:  5a257cd =  56:  3426788 Hold xt tests up to the same standards\n 57:  668a004 =  57:  78a1c52 Separate import preamble consistently\n 58:  a03a774 =  58:  b0b4862 Add recent tests to MANIFEST\n 59:  dfa15b3 =  59:  bf819c9 xt/*.t: address quirks for older perls\n 60:  0d8d810 !  60:  8ad4e05 xt/tree-search-cmd: Finish regression test\n--- a/0d8d81003e71fbf44ba6c80f8e2c3f34ad740ab0\t2026-05-28 19:28:58.000000000 +0000\n+++ b/8ad4e057b8677069f25486703e6a1f3f46213556\t2026-05-28 19:28:58.000000000 +0000\n\@\@ -4,9 +4,11 \@\@\n committer Ethan Meng <ethan\@rapidcow.org> 1779996538 -0500\n \n xt/tree-search-cmd: Finish regression test\n \n-Regression test for commit 87e5c21, where we replaced\n+[Message by Claude]\n+\n+Regression test for commit 7a9ae69, where we replaced\n File::Find with true lexicographic find.  Root tree is\n borrowed from the neighboring xt/tree-search.t.\n \n (I had totally forgotten about \"conclude\", so props to\n 61:  50619d8 =  61:  0af5c03 xt/tree-search-cmd: basic load test\n 62:  fb4613e =  62:  7567e74 Initialize tree-search-cmd boilerplate\n 63:  1231bef =  63:  18dfb4f Copy \"t/lib/test-functions.sh\" from HashTree test\n 64:  9824040 =  64:  4e80d88 tree-search: sanity check on self\n 65:  87e5c21 =  65:  7a9ae69 tree-search find: roll our own lexicograpical sort\n 66:  477409e =  66:  35d90cb xlib/tree-search: Fix a few other spots\n 67:  17e5196 =  67:  d82d131 Just import all the names please\n 68:  fce804a =  68:  739ccca Expose as BST_{leap,delv} as subcommands\n 69:  94da660 =  69:  476eda8 tree-search tests fixup\n 70:  c752079 =  70:  1e7c8bc xlib/tree-search: fix four bugs; xt/tree-search: add tests\n 71:  2a76a85 =  71:  e6c3bb1 BST_leap and BST_delv proof of concept\n 72:  010e040 =  72:  1fb49ae Begin another experiment\n 73:  b8cad6f =  73:  b986c70 Grammar again\n 74:  e032900 =  74:  358f519 01ARRAY: continued for right search\n 75:  e2dcbd1 =  75:  d2b319d file => document\n 76:  7a928dd =  76:  b2c898f Add dummy files for srcdocs\n 77:  0a310c8 =  77:  50b3d26 semicolons please\n 78:  97bda1b =  78:  85bb9f5 Get rid of useless +n -n tests\n 79:  2743324 =  79:  a8448d4 parenthesize this SKIP for consistency\n 80:  e26fa13 =  80:  0fe077e t/mean.t: skip boundary tests when no PERL_PRESERVE_IVUV\n 81:  db4fed4 =  81:  d58420c Require Test-Simple 0.94\n 82:  d3ff2d4 =  82:  a5bae1c Explicitly return in tied array getters\n 83:  1c1fef6 =  83:  7a33418 Chained inequality is new to perl v5.32.0\n 84:  0227ca4 =  84:  e9a0165 Test ARRAY form\n 85:  71991c7 =  85:  7e5b1a8 I think mean.t should actually be 20\n 86:  0bd20fb =  86:  657ce6b t/mean.t: load Math::BigInt optionally\n 87:  8590c05 =  87:  f9df78c Prefix t/mean.t with \"10\"\n 88:  0bb6b4f =  88:  fd99e58 Author tests get the load test too\n 89:  d4479a3 =  89:  6ab48fe t/mean.t: make syntax work\n 90:  0a7cb7f =  90:  fec80a6 mean test with bigint!\n 91:  fab7690 =  91:  c18361a Mean test\n 92:  ba157bc =  92:  9db1ec0 Append most recent runs to the files\n 93:  5296c1a =  93:  70fb80b Benchmark one last time\n 94:  f2d0cbb =  94:  2ba5b61 I think string comparison is a bit expensive for \$ref\n 95:  e67bc71 =  95:  f6154f6 Benchmark results (again)\n 96:  542c1bb =  96:  7325145 peel off ARRAY wrapper\n 97:  c203d9a =  97:  e87bfd5 Report benchmark results\n 98:  35a356d =  98:  d57fa99 ... and please S::S[2] don't be slower\n 99:  5a10339 =  99:  55d1bd9 Add lzero.pl test results\n100:  46f335e = 100:  28a172a Maybe we should factor out anon subs\n101:  ef10f68 = 101:  e0105ca Test match for one bound only\n102:  ef15e6d = 102:  0a9588b Check \$INC{\$filename} is defined, not just existing\n103:  1f9d326 = 103:  66a4290 Re-run results against LINEAR baseline\n104:  9aa60c6 = 104:  abb291b Align arguments in the b*srch2 variants\n105:  e3602d1 = 105:  c5bc3ce Add LINEAR baseline to make myself feel better\n106:  7cdc0d9 = 106:  be6c4c9 Exclude bench/ from MANIFEST (but not git export)\n107:  3a200a3 = 107:  59c8adc Re-run benchmark with List::MoreUtils::XS\n108:  c209d42 = 108:  3194024 We can actually replace \"if (!\" with \"unless (\"?\n109:  35d7a00 ! 109:  db2a69d Move explicit index form check up\n--- a/35d7a00f4dcb604baa0c016119aa569895a53e91\t2026-05-23 19:13:27.000000000 +0000\n+++ b/db2a69d856cf9e4dbf1d43cddbc2231a0bdd9139\t2026-05-23